---
// Landing page for BFSI investors and bank executives.
// Three parts only: 1. Why RE-ViVE for banks, 2. How effective, 3. Client references.
// Shared site header and footer (chrome.css + banking nav layers); page styles in /assets/css/landing.css.
// The previous home page is kept in the backups folder next to site\.
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const CONTACT = "https://re-vive.com/company/contact";
const EMAIL = "connect@revivetoday.com";
---
<Layout title="RE-ViVE | Execution Intelligence for Banks" description="Banking processes are too complex and too regulated for statistical estimates. RE-ViVE deterministically reconstructs how every loan, payment and case actually ran, from records the bank already keeps, without asking how the process is supposed to work." current="/">
<Fragment slot="head">
<link href="/images/favicon.svg" rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml"/>
<link as="font" crossorigin href="/fonts/inter-var-latin.woff2" rel="preload" type="font/woff2"/>
<link href="/assets/css/chrome.css" rel="stylesheet"/>
<link href="/assets/css/banking-nav-v4.css" rel="stylesheet"/>
<link href="/assets/css/banking-production-v7.css" rel="stylesheet"/>
<link href="/assets/css/landing.css" rel="stylesheet"/>
</Fragment>


<main id="main">

  <!-- 1. Why RE-ViVE for banks -->
  <section class="lp-section lp-why">
    <div class="lp-shell">
      <p class="lp-eyebrow">Why RE-ViVE for banks</p>
      <h1 class="lp-h1">Every loan. Every payment. Every case. <span>Exactly as it ran.</span></h1>
      <p class="lp-lead">Banks can't run on estimates. Other tools infer the process from statistical models. RE-ViVE reconstructs exactly how every transaction ran, from records the bank already keeps, and never has to ask how the process is supposed to work.</p>

      <p class="lp-only">What only RE-ViVE brings together</p>
      <div class="lp-pillars">
        <div class="lp-pillar">
          <h3>Exact, not estimated</h3>
          <p>Deterministic reconstruction, not statistical inference. Every figure traces back to a real transaction that an examiner can open.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lp-pillar">
          <h3>Zero process interviews</h3>
          <p>No workshops, process models or SOP mapping. The bank gives read-only access, and the process map emerges from the evidence.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lp-pillar">
          <h3>Built for bank complexity</h3>
          <p>Parallel checks told apart from rework, 30 to 100 business dimensions, and workflows that change quarter to quarter, all on one foundation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lp-pillar">
          <h3>Deploys anywhere</h3>
          <p>On-premises, private cloud or the bank's own cloud. Source access stays read-only and nothing is written back.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. How effective (cost and time) -->
  <section class="lp-section lp-effect">
    <div class="lp-shell">
      <p class="lp-eyebrow">How effective</p>
      <h2 class="lp-h2">Weeks, not quarters. Hours of the bank's time, not months.</h2>
      <p class="lp-lead">A full view of how the bank really runs, in about two weeks, with no process modeling and no new operational system.</p>

      <div class="lp-stats">
        <div class="lp-stat">
          <strong>~10 days</strong>
          <span>Business days from data access to the first execution view</span>
        </div>
        <div class="lp-stat">
          <strong>2–4 hrs</strong>
          <span>Subject-matter time from the bank to establish context</span>
        </div>
        <div class="lp-stat">
          <strong>100+ <em>vs</em> 0</strong>
          <span>Workflows reconstructed in a head-to-head, while the alternative had none completed after about three months on comparable data</span>
        </div>
        <div class="lp-stat">
          <strong>~30%</strong>
          <span>Faster customer onboarding identified from one bank's own records</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="lp-reach"><strong>Built in banking. Ready for every workflow and every AI agent.</strong> The same foundation covers onboarding, payments, lending, cards, compliance and capital markets, and extends to insurance, healthcare and the AI agents now entering these workflows.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. Client references -->
  <section class="lp-section lp-refs">
    <div class="lp-shell">
      <p class="lp-eyebrow">Client references</p>
      <h2 class="lp-h2">Banks see exactly where time and money are lost, and what to fix first.</h2>
      <p class="lp-lead">Proven with multiple banks, in live engagements and pilots, and selected in competitive evaluations against established enterprise vendors.</p>

      <div class="lp-cards">
        <article class="lp-card">
          <p class="lp-card-tag">Large multinational bank · Customer onboarding</p>
          <h3>About 30% faster onboarding identified</h3>
          <p>8.28 million events across 953,000 requests. 10 of the 16.6 days in an average request were rework, concentrated in four activities.</p>
          <p class="lp-card-foot">Findings in two weeks from about 2 hours of subject-matter time.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="lp-card">
          <p class="lp-card-tag">Global payments and custody bank · Investigations</p>
          <h3>The 3.6% of cases behind most of the aging, named</h3>
          <p>269,000 investigations and 550,000 messages. One reported average split into two real populations, each with an SLA it can meet.</p>
          <p class="lp-card-foot">From read-only extracts and one month of production data.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="lp-card">
          <p class="lp-card-tag">Bank service operations · SLA exposure</p>
          <h3>Nearly 100 service workflows made visible</h3>
          <p>Evidence spread across spreadsheets, workflow platforms and custom applications, organized into observed paths, SLA behavior and intervention patterns.</p>
          <p class="lp-card-foot">About 10 business days from about 4 hours of subject-matter time.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="lp-note">Opportunities measured from each bank's own records. Clients are not named.</p>

      <div class="lp-cta">
        <h3>See it on a live demo, or on one of your own workflows.</h3>
        <div class="lp-cta-row">
          <a class="lp-btn" href={CONTACT}>Request a demo</a>
          <a class="lp-link" href={"mailto:" + EMAIL}>{EMAIL}</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="lp-more">Want the detail behind these claims? <a class="lp-link" href="/how-it-works">See how it works in a bank →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>

</Layout>
